      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bangkok’s canals, once the main transport arteries, have been largely replaced by road traffic, yet the city still retains a network of historic khlong.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bangkok",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Giant Swing and Erawan Shrine showcase Hindu influences that are deeply woven into Bangkok’s cultural fabric.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bangkok",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Bangkok houses Thailand’s five oldest universities, including Chulalongkorn founded in 1917, making it an educational hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bangkok",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
